    skos:definition "Constraint programming solver built on satisfiability: one declares a model (integer and Boolean variables, linear and global constraints, objective), the solver solves it and tells whether the returned solution is proved optimal. Its architecture chains presolve, propagation, a clause-learning SAT engine and linear relaxation."@en,
